-- FORK F48 (see NOTES.md, Fork register)
`s 253(4) the person is one of the persons guilty of the offence` MEANS
    IF `the person is the person making the offer` OR (`what section 253(4)(b) answers` EQUALS JUST TRUE) OR (`what section 253(4)(c) answers` EQUALS JUST TRUE) OR (`what section 253(4)(d) answers` EQUALS JUST TRUE) OR (`what section 253(4)(e) answers` EQUALS JUST TRUE) OR (`what section 253(4)(f) answers` EQUALS JUST TRUE) OR (`what section 253(4)(g) answers` EQUALS JUST TRUE)
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (list not closed): "The persons guilty of the offence are" is a list of seven kinds and not closed with "only"

-- s 253(1), the offence. "even if such persons ... were not involved" removes any need for the person's own part. Only an answer JUST TRUE counts for the defence of section 255.
-- src:41007 | the persons referred to in subsection (4) shall be guilty of an offence
-- src:41008 | even if such persons, unless otherwise specified, were not involved in
-- src:41009 | the making of the false or misleading statement or the omission, and
-- src:41010 | shall be liable on conviction to a fine not exceeding $150,000 or to
-- src:41011 | imprisonment for a term not exceeding 2 years or to both and, in the
-- src:41012 | case of a continuing offence, to a further fine not exceeding $15,000
-- src:41013 | for every day or part of a day during which the offence continues after
-- src:41014 | conviction.
@ref s 253(1) (the offence) (src:41007-41014)
GIVEN
    `what section 253(1) answers` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN @desc What does the function `s 253(1) the false or misleading statement or omission is present` answer for the prospectus or profile statement? (JUST TRUE, JUST FALSE, or NOTHING if you do not know.)
    `what section 253(3) answers` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN @desc What does the function `s 253(3) the person does not contravene subsection (1)` answer for the person? (JUST TRUE, JUST FALSE, or NOTHING if you do not know.)
    `what section 253(4) answers` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN @desc What does the function `s 253(4) the person is one of the persons guilty of the offence` answer for the person? (JUST TRUE, JUST FALSE, or NOTHING if you do not know.)
    `what section 255 answers` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN @desc What does the function `s 255 the person has a defence` answer for the person? (JUST TRUE, JUST FALSE, or NOTHING if you do not know.)
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
-- FORK F49 (see NOTES.md, Fork register)
`s 253(1) the person is guilty of an offence` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF (`what section 253(1) answers` EQUALS JUST FALSE)
        THEN JUST FALSE  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Where an offer of securities or securities-based derivatives contracts is made in or accompanied by a prospectus or profile statement"
        IF (`what section 253(3) answers` EQUALS JUST TRUE) OR (`what section 255 answers` EQUALS JUST TRUE)
        THEN JUST FALSE  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "A person does not contravene subsection (1) if"
        IF (`what section 253(1) answers` EQUALS JUST TRUE) AND (`what section 253(4) answers` EQUALS JUST TRUE)
        THEN JUST TRUE
        IF (`what section 253(1) answers` EQUALS JUST TRUE)
        THEN NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "the persons referred to in subsection (4) shall be guilty of an offence"  -- SPLIT-SITE (i)
        OTHERWISE NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (silent): an answer under subsection (1) was not worked out

@ref s 253(1) (the penalty) (src:41007-41014)
GIVETH A Penalty
`s 253(1) the penalty for the offence` MEANS
    Penalty OF 150000, 24, TRUE, 15000  -- a fine not exceeding $150,000, or imprisonment not exceeding 2 years, or both; a further fine not exceeding $15,000 for every day or part of a day the offence continues after conviction

-- s 253(5): "remedial action includes" (an includes); "reckless" for subsection (4)(d)(iii) and (e)(iii).
-- src:41129 | (5) For the purposes of subsection (4) and this subsection —
-- src:41131 | (a) remedial action includes any of the following:
-- src:41133 | (i) preventing the statement from being included, or
-- src:41134 | having the information or circumstance included, in
-- src:41135 | the prospectus or profile statement, as the case may
-- src:41136 | be;
-- src:41138 | (ii) procuring the lodgment of a supplementary or
-- src:41139 | replacement prospectus under section 241; and
@ref s 253(5)(a) (src:41129-41139)
GIVEN
    `the action prevents the statement from being included, or has the information or circumstance included` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the action prevent the statement from being included, or have the information or circumstance included, in the prospectus or profile statement?
    `the action procures the lodgment of a supplementary or replacement prospectus under section 241` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the action procure the lodgment of a supplementary or replacement prospectus under section 241?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
-- FORK F50 (see NOTES.md, Fork register)
`s 253(5)(a) the action is remedial action` MEANS
    IF `the action prevents the statement from being included, or has the information or circumstance included` OR `the action procures the lodgment of a supplementary or replacement prospectus under section 241`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (includes): "remedial action includes any of the following"

-- src:41141 | (b) a person is reckless as to the matter referred to in
-- src:41142 | subsection (4)(d)(iii) or (e)(iii) if, having been put upon
-- src:41143 | inquiry that the statement to be, or which has been,
-- src:41144 | included in the prospectus or profile statement is likely to
-- src:41145 | be false or misleading, that the information or
-- src:41146 | circumstance is likely to be required to be included in
-- src:41147 | that document, or that there is likely to be an omission to
-- src:41148 | state the information or circumstance in that document, the
-- src:41149 | person fails to —
-- src:41151 | (i) make all inquiries as are reasonable in the
-- src:41152 | circumstances to verify this; and
-- src:41154 | (ii) take such remedial action as is appropriate in the
-- src:41155 | circumstances without delay, if such action is
-- src:41156 | warranted by the outcome of the inquiries.
@ref s 253(5)(b) (src:41141-41156)
GIVEN
    `the person is put upon inquiry that the statement is likely to be false or misleading, that the information or circumstance is likely to be required, or that there is likely to be an omission` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you put upon inquiry that the statement to be, or which has been, included in the prospectus or profile statement is likely to be false or misleading, that the information or circumstance is likely to be required to be included in that document, or that there is likely to be an omission to state it?
    `the person makes all inquiries as are reasonable in the circumstances to verify this` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do you make all inquiries as are reasonable in the circumstances to verify this?
    `the person takes such remedial action as is appropriate in the circumstances without delay` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do you take such remedial action as is appropriate in the circumstances without delay?
    `remedial action is warranted by the outcome of the inquiries` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is remedial action warranted by the outcome of the inquiries?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
-- FORK F50 (see NOTES.md, Fork register)
`s 253(5)(b) the person is reckless` MEANS
    IF `the person is put upon inquiry that the statement is likely to be false or misleading, that the information or circumstance is likely to be required, or that there is likely to be an omission` AND ((NOT `the person makes all inquiries as are reasonable in the circumstances to verify this`) OR (`remedial action is warranted by the outcome of the inquiries` AND (NOT `the person takes such remedial action as is appropriate in the circumstances without delay`)))
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "a person is reckless as to the matter referred to in subsection (4)(d)(iii) or (e)(iii) if, having been put upon inquiry"

-- src:41158 | (6) For the purposes of this section, any reference to a statement
-- src:41159 | includes a reference to any information presented, regardless of
-- src:41160 | whether such information is in text or otherwise.
@ref s 253(6) (src:41158-41160)
GIVEN
    `the item is a statement` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the item a statement?
    `the item is information presented, whether in text or otherwise` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the item information presented, regardless of whether it is in text or otherwise?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 253(6) the item is a statement for the purposes of this section` MEANS
    IF `the item is a statement` OR `the item is information presented, whether in text or otherwise`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (includes): "any reference to a statement includes a reference to any information presented, regardless of whether such information is in text or otherwise"

§ `s 254: civil liability for false or misleading statements`

-- s 254(1), the facts: the "Where" block, as at section 253(1) (section 254(1)(c)(ii) says "required by section 243").
-- src:41164 | 254.—(1) Where an offer of securities or securities‑based
-- src:41165 | derivatives contracts is made in or accompanied by a prospectus or
-- src:41166 | profile statement, or, in the case of an offer referred to in section 280,
-- src:41167 | where a prospectus or profile statement is prepared and issued in
-- src:41168 | relation to the offer, and —
-- src:41173 | (a) a false or misleading statement is contained in —
-- src:41175 | (i) the prospectus or the profile statement; or
-- src:41177 | (ii) any application form for the securities or
-- src:41178 | securities‑based derivatives contracts;
-- src:41180 | (b) there is an omission to state any information required to be
-- src:41181 | included in the prospectus under section 243 or there is an
-- src:41182 | omission to state any information required to be included
-- src:41183 | in the profile statement under section 246, as the case may
-- src:41184 | be; or
-- src:41186 | (c) there is an omission to state a new circumstance that —
-- src:41188 | (i) has arisen since the prospectus or the profile
-- src:41189 | statement was lodged with the Authority; and
-- src:41191 | (ii) would have been required by section 243 to be
-- src:41192 | included in the prospectus, or required to be included
-- src:41193 | in the profile statement under section 246 (as the case
-- src:41194 | may be) if it had arisen before the prospectus or the
-- src:41195 | profile statement was lodged with the Authority,
@ref s 254(1) (the facts) (src:41164-41195)
GIVEN
    `an offer is made in or accompanied by a prospectus or profile statement` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is an offer of securities or securities-based derivatives contracts made in, or accompanied by, a prospectus or profile statement?
    `the offer is an offer referred to in section 280` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the offer an offer referred to in section 280?
    `a prospectus or profile statement is prepared and issued in relation to the offer` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is a prospectus or profile statement prepared and issued in relation to the offer?
    `a false or misleading statement is contained in the prospectus, the profile statement or an application form` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is a false or misleading statement contained in the prospectus, in the profile statement, or in any application form for the securities or securities-based derivatives contracts?
    `there is an omission to state any information required to be included in the prospectus under section 243 or in the profile statement under section 246` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is there an omission to state any information required to be included in the prospectus under section 243, or in the profile statement under section 246, as the case may be?
    `there is an omission to state a new circumstance that has arisen since the prospectus or profile statement was lodged` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is there an omission to state a new circumstance that has arisen since the prospectus or the profile statement was lodged with the Authority?
    `the new circumstance would have been required to be included had it arisen before lodgment` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Would the new circumstance have been required to be included in the prospectus under section 243, or in the profile statement under section 246, if it had arisen before the prospectus or the profile statement was lodged with the Authority?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
-- FORK F44 (see NOTES.md, Fork register)
`s 254(1) the false or misleading statement or omission is present` MEANS
    IF (`an offer is made in or accompanied by a prospectus or profile statement` OR (`the offer is an offer referred to in section 280` AND `a prospectus or profile statement is prepared and issued in relation to the offer`)) AND (`a false or misleading statement is contained in the prospectus, the profile statement or an application form` OR `there is an omission to state any information required to be included in the prospectus under section 243 or in the profile statement under section 246` OR (`there is an omission to state a new circumstance that has arisen since the prospectus or profile statement was lodged` AND `the new circumstance would have been required to be included had it arisen before lodgment`))
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Where an offer of securities or securities-based derivatives contracts is made in or accompanied by a prospectus or profile statement, or, in the case of an offer referred to in section 280, where a prospectus or profile statement is prepared and issued in relation to the offer, and"

-- s 254(2): the same deeming as section 253(2) ("makes").
-- src:41206 | (2) For the purposes of subsection (1), a false or misleading
-- src:41207 | statement about a future matter (including the doing of, or the refusal
-- src:41208 | to do, an act) is taken to have been made if a person makes the
-- src:41209 | statement without having reasonable grounds for making the
-- src:41210 | statement.
@ref s 254(2) (src:41206-41210)
GIVEN
    `the statement is about a future matter, including the doing of, or the refusal to do, an act` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the statement about a future matter (including the doing of, or the refusal to do, an act)?
    `the person makes the statement` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the person make the statement?
    `the person had reasonable grounds for making the statement` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the person have reasonable grounds for making the statement?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
-- FORK F45 (see NOTES.md, Fork register)
`s 254(2) a false or misleading statement about a future matter is taken to have been made` MEANS
    IF `the statement is about a future matter, including the doing of, or the refusal to do, an act` AND `the person makes the statement` AND (NOT `the person had reasonable grounds for making the statement`)
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "a false or misleading statement about a future matter (including the doing of, or the refusal to do, an act) is taken to have been made if a person makes the statement without having reasonable grounds for making the statement"

-- s 254(3): the persons liable. Each paragraph is a function; the combiner follows.
-- src:41216 | (b) where the person making the offer is an entity —
-- src:41218 | (i) each director or equivalent person of the entity; and
-- src:41223 | (ii) if the entity is also the issuer, each person who is, and
-- src:41224 | who has consented to be, named in the prospectus or
-- src:41225 | profile statement as a proposed director or an
-- src:41226 | equivalent person of the entity;
@ref s 254(3)(b) (src:41216-41226)
GIVEN
    `the person making the offer is an entity` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the person making the offer an entity?
    `the person is a director or an equivalent person of the entity` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you a director or an equivalent person of the entity?
    `the entity is also the issuer` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the entity also the issuer?
    `the person is, and has consented to be, named in the prospectus or profile statement as a proposed director or an equivalent person of the entity` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you, and have you consented to be, named in the prospectus or profile statement as a proposed director or an equivalent person of the entity?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
-- FORK F47 (see NOTES.md, Fork register)
`s 254(3)(b) the person is a director or proposed director of the entity making the offer` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF (NOT `the person making the offer is an entity`)
        THEN JUST FALSE  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "where the person making the offer is an entity"
        IF `the person is a director or an equivalent person of the entity` OR (`the entity is also the issuer` AND `the person is, and has consented to be, named in the prospectus or profile statement as a proposed director or an equivalent person of the entity`)
        THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "each director or equivalent person of the entity"

-- src:41228 | (c) where the issuer is controlled by the person making the
-- src:41229 | offer, one or more of the related parties of the person
-- src:41230 | making the offer, or the person making the offer and one or
-- src:41231 | more of that person’s related parties —
-- src:41233 | (i) the issuer;
-- src:41235 | (ii) each director or equivalent person of the issuer; and
-- src:41237 | (iii) each person who is, and who has consented to be,
-- src:41238 | named in the prospectus or the profile statement as a
-- src:41239 | proposed director or an equivalent person of the
-- src:41240 | issuer;
@ref s 254(3)(c) (src:41228-41240)
GIVEN
    `the issuer is controlled by the person making the offer, one or more of that person's related parties, or the person and one or more of those related parties` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the issuer controlled by the person making the offer, by one or more of the related parties of the person making the offer, or by the person making the offer and one or more of that person's related parties?
    `the person is the issuer` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you the issuer?
    `the person is a director or an equivalent person of the issuer` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you a director or an equivalent person of the issuer?
    `the person is, and has consented to be, named in the prospectus or profile statement as a proposed director or an equivalent person of the issuer` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you, and have you consented to be, named in the prospectus or profile statement as a proposed director or an equivalent person of the issuer?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
-- FORK F47 (see NOTES.md, Fork register)
`s 254(3)(c) the person is the issuer or a director or proposed director of the issuer` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF (NOT `the issuer is controlled by the person making the offer, one or more of that person's related parties, or the person and one or more of those related parties`)
        THEN JUST FALSE  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "where the issuer is controlled by the person making the offer"
        IF `the person is the issuer` OR `the person is a director or an equivalent person of the issuer` OR `the person is, and has consented to be, named in the prospectus or profile statement as a proposed director or an equivalent person of the issuer`
        THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "the issuer" ... "each director or equivalent person of the issuer" ... "each person who is, and who has consented to be, named in the prospectus or the profile statement as a proposed director or an equivalent person of the issuer"

