    IF `the item is a statement` OR `the item is information presented, whether in text or otherwise`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (includes): "any reference to a statement includes a reference to any information presented, regardless of whether such information is in text or otherwise"

-- s 254(5): a limitation. "No action ... may be commenced after the expiration of 6 years" is a bar whose period the text fixes in its own words: JUST FALSE inside it, JUST TRUE after it (fork F52).
-- src:41287 | (5) No action under subsection (1) may be commenced after the
-- src:41288 | expiration of 6 years from the date on which the cause of action arose.
@ref s 254(5) (src:41287-41288)
GIVEN
    `the date on which the cause of action arose` IS A DATE @desc On what date did the cause of action arise?
    `the date on which the action is commenced` IS A DATE @desc On what date is the action commenced?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
-- FORK F52 (see NOTES.md, Fork register)
`s 254(5) the action may not be commenced` MEANS
    IF `the date on which the action is commenced` AT MOST (`period: the last day of a period after` `the date on which the cause of action arose` 6 Years)
    THEN JUST FALSE  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "after the expiration of 6 years from the date on which the cause of action arose"
    ELSE JUST TRUE

-- s 254(6): a flat negative.
-- src:41290 | (6) This section does not affect any liability that a person has under
-- src:41291 | any other law.
@ref s 254(6) (src:41290-41291)
GIVEN
    `the liability arises under another law` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the liability the person has arise under any other law?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 254(6) this section affects a liability under another law` MEANS
    IF `the liability arises under another law`
    THEN JUST FALSE  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "This section does not affect any liability that a person has under any other law"
    ELSE NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "any liability that a person has under any other law" says nothing of a liability under this Act

§ `s 255: defences`

-- s 255 defences are delegated defences (the ruling of 2026-11-05, `inputs/ENCODING-GUIDE.md:94`, (b)): JUST TRUE when the person proves what the paragraph asks; JUST FALSE when not, worded "this section gives no defence on these facts"; NOTHING when the scope (the kind of person or liability) is outside the paragraph (fork F53).
-- src:41295 | 255.—(1) A person referred to in section 253(4)(a), (b) or (c) is not
-- src:41296 | liable under section 253(1), and a person referred to in section 254(3)
-- src:41297 | is not liable under section 254(1), only because of a false or
-- src:41298 | misleading statement in a prospectus or a profile statement if the
-- src:41299 | person proves that the person —
-- src:41301 | (a) made all inquiries (if any) that were reasonable in the
-- src:41302 | circumstances; and
-- src:41304 | (b) after doing so, believed on reasonable grounds that the
-- src:41305 | statement was not false or misleading.
@ref s 255(1) (src:41295-41305)
GIVEN
    `the person is referred to in section 253(4)(a), (b) or (c) and the liability is under section 253(1), or the person is referred to in section 254(3) and the liability is under section 254(1)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the person one referred to in section 253(4)(a), (b) or (c) and the liability one under section 253(1), or one referred to in section 254(3) and the liability one under section 254(1)?
    `the liability is only because of a false or misleading statement in a prospectus or a profile statement` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the liability only because of a false or misleading statement in a prospectus or a profile statement?
    `the person proves that the person made all inquiries (if any) that were reasonable in the circumstances` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the person prove that the person made all inquiries (if any) that were reasonable in the circumstances?
    `the person proves that after doing so the person believed on reasonable grounds that the statement was not false or misleading` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the person prove that, after doing so, the person believed on reasonable grounds that the statement was not false or misleading?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
-- FORK F53 (see NOTES.md, Fork register)
`s 255(1) this section gives a defence for the false or misleading statement` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF (NOT (`the person is referred to in section 253(4)(a), (b) or (c) and the liability is under section 253(1), or the person is referred to in section 254(3) and the liability is under section 254(1)` AND `the liability is only because of a false or misleading statement in a prospectus or a profile statement`))
        THEN NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "A person referred to in section 253(4)(a), (b) or (c) is not liable under section 253(1), and a person referred to in section 254(3) is not liable under section 254(1), only because of a false or misleading statement in a prospectus or a profile statement"
        IF `the person proves that the person made all inquiries (if any) that were reasonable in the circumstances` AND `the person proves that after doing so the person believed on reasonable grounds that the statement was not false or misleading`
        THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "if the person proves that the person" ... "made all inquiries (if any) that were reasonable in the circumstances"

-- src:41307 | (2) A person referred to in section 253(4)(a), (b) or (c) is not liable
-- src:41308 | under section 253(1), and a person referred to in section 254(3) is not
-- src:41309 | liable under section 254(1), only because of an omission from a
-- src:41310 | prospectus or a profile statement in relation to a particular matter if
-- src:41311 | the person proves that the person —
-- src:41313 | (a) made all inquiries (if any) that were reasonable in the
-- src:41314 | circumstances; and
-- src:41319 | (b) after doing so, believed on reasonable grounds that there
-- src:41320 | was no omission from the prospectus or profile statement
-- src:41321 | in relation to that matter.
@ref s 255(2) (src:41307-41321)
GIVEN
    `the person is referred to in section 253(4)(a), (b) or (c) and the liability is under section 253(1), or the person is referred to in section 254(3) and the liability is under section 254(1)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the person one referred to in section 253(4)(a), (b) or (c) and the liability one under section 253(1), or one referred to in section 254(3) and the liability one under section 254(1)?
    `the liability is only because of an omission from a prospectus or a profile statement in relation to a particular matter` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the liability only because of an omission from a prospectus or a profile statement in relation to a particular matter?
    `the person proves that the person made all inquiries (if any) that were reasonable in the circumstances` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the person prove that the person made all inquiries (if any) that were reasonable in the circumstances?
    `the person proves that after doing so the person believed on reasonable grounds that there was no omission from the prospectus or profile statement in relation to that matter` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the person prove that, after doing so, the person believed on reasonable grounds that there was no omission from the prospectus or profile statement in relation to that matter?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
-- FORK F53 (see NOTES.md, Fork register)
`s 255(2) this section gives a defence for the omission` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF (NOT (`the person is referred to in section 253(4)(a), (b) or (c) and the liability is under section 253(1), or the person is referred to in section 254(3) and the liability is under section 254(1)` AND `the liability is only because of an omission from a prospectus or a profile statement in relation to a particular matter`))
        THEN NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "A person referred to in section 253(4)(a), (b) or (c) is not liable under section 253(1), and a person referred to in section 254(3) is not liable under section 254(1), only because of an omission from a prospectus or a profile statement in relation to a particular matter"
        IF `the person proves that the person made all inquiries (if any) that were reasonable in the circumstances` AND `the person proves that after doing so the person believed on reasonable grounds that there was no omission from the prospectus or profile statement in relation to that matter`
        THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "if the person proves that the person" ... "made all inquiries (if any) that were reasonable in the circumstances"

-- src:41323 | (3) A person is not liable under section 253(1) or 254(1) only
-- src:41324 | because of a false or misleading statement in, or an omission from, a
-- src:41325 | prospectus or a profile statement if the person proves that the person
-- src:41326 | placed reasonable reliance on information given to the person by —
-- src:41328 | (a) if the person is an entity, someone other than —
-- src:41330 | (i) a director or an equivalent person; or
-- src:41332 | (ii) an employee or agent,
-- src:41334 | (a) of the entity; or
-- src:41336 | (b) if the person is an individual, someone other than an
-- src:41337 | employee or agent of the individual.
@ref s 255(3) (src:41323-41337)
GIVEN
    `the liability is only because of a false or misleading statement in, or an omission from, a prospectus or profile statement` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the liability under section 253(1) or 254(1) only because of a false or misleading statement in, or an omission from, a prospectus or a profile statement?
    `the person is an entity` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the person an entity?
    `the person is an individual` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the person an individual?
    `the person proves reasonable reliance on information given to the person` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the person prove that the person placed reasonable reliance on information given to the person?
    `the informant is a director or an equivalent person of the entity` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the one who gave the information a director or an equivalent person of the entity?
    `the informant is an employee or agent of the entity` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the one who gave the information an employee or agent of the entity?
    `the informant is an employee or agent of the individual` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the one who gave the information an employee or agent of the individual?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
-- FORK F53 (see NOTES.md, Fork register)
`s 255(3) this section gives a defence for reasonable reliance on information` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF (NOT `the liability is only because of a false or misleading statement in, or an omission from, a prospectus or profile statement`)
        THEN NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "A person is not liable under section 253(1) or 254(1) only because of a false or misleading statement in, or an omission from, a prospectus or a profile statement"
        IF `the person proves reasonable reliance on information given to the person` AND ((`the person is an entity` AND (NOT (`the informant is a director or an equivalent person of the entity` OR `the informant is an employee or agent of the entity`))) OR (`the person is an individual` AND (NOT `the informant is an employee or agent of the individual`)))
        THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "if the person proves that the person placed reasonable reliance on information given to the person by"

-- src:41339 | (4) For the purposes of subsection (3), a person is not the agent of
-- src:41340 | an entity or individual merely because that person performs a
-- src:41341 | particular professional or advisory function for the entity or
-- src:41342 | individual.
@ref s 255(4) (src:41339-41342)
GIVEN
    `the person merely performs a particular professional or advisory function for the entity or individual` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the person merely perform a particular professional or advisory function for the entity or individual?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
-- FORK F53 (see NOTES.md, Fork register)
`s 255(4) the person is an agent of the entity or individual` MEANS
    IF `the person merely performs a particular professional or advisory function for the entity or individual`
    THEN JUST FALSE  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "a person is not the agent of an entity or individual merely because that person performs a particular professional or advisory function for the entity or individual"
    ELSE NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "merely because that person performs a particular professional or advisory function" says nothing of a person who does more

-- src:41344 | (5) A person who is named in a prospectus or a profile statement
-- src:41345 | as —
-- src:41347 | (a) a proposed director or an equivalent person of the issuer, or
-- src:41348 | an issue manager or underwriter;
-- src:41350 | (b) having made a statement included in the prospectus or the
-- src:41351 | profile statement; or
-- src:41353 | (c) having made a statement on the basis of which a statement
-- src:41354 | is included in the prospectus or the profile statement,
-- src:41356 | is not liable under section 253(1) or 254(1) only because of a false or
-- src:41357 | misleading statement in, or an omission from, the prospectus or the
-- src:41358 | profile statement if the person proves that the person publicly
-- src:41359 | withdrew the person’s consent to being named in the prospectus or
-- src:41360 | the profile statement in that way.
@ref s 255(5) (src:41344-41360)
GIVEN
    `the person is named in the prospectus or profile statement as a proposed director, an issue manager or underwriter, a person who made a statement included in it, or a person on whose statement a statement in it is based` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you named in the prospectus or a profile statement as a proposed director or an equivalent person of the issuer, an issue manager or underwriter, as having made a statement included in it, or as having made a statement on the basis of which a statement is included in it?
    `the liability is only because of a false or misleading statement in, or an omission from, the prospectus or profile statement` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the liability under section 253(1) or 254(1) only because of a false or misleading statement in, or an omission from, the prospectus or the profile statement?
    `the person proves that the person publicly withdrew the person's consent to being named in that way` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the person prove that the person publicly withdrew the person's consent to being named in the prospectus or the profile statement in that way?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
-- FORK F53 (see NOTES.md, Fork register)
`s 255(5) this section gives a defence for publicly withdrawing consent` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF (NOT (`the person is named in the prospectus or profile statement as a proposed director, an issue manager or underwriter, a person who made a statement included in it, or a person on whose statement a statement in it is based` AND `the liability is only because of a false or misleading statement in, or an omission from, the prospectus or profile statement`))
        THEN NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "A person who is named in a prospectus or a profile statement as"
        IF `the person proves that the person publicly withdrew the person's consent to being named in that way`
        THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "if the person proves that the person publicly withdrew the person's consent to being named in the prospectus or the profile statement in that way"

-- src:41362 | (6) A person is not liable under section 253(1) or 254(1) only
-- src:41363 | because of a new circumstance that has arisen since the prospectus or
-- src:41368 | the profile statement was lodged with the Authority if the person
-- src:41369 | proves that the person was not aware of the matter.
@ref s 255(6) (src:41362-41369)
GIVEN
    `the liability is only because of a new circumstance that has arisen since the prospectus or profile statement was lodged` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the liability under section 253(1) or 254(1) only because of a new circumstance that has arisen since the prospectus or the profile statement was lodged with the Authority?
    `the person proves that the person was not aware of the matter` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the person prove that the person was not aware of the matter?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
-- FORK F53 (see NOTES.md, Fork register)
`s 255(6) this section gives a defence for not being aware of a new circumstance` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF (NOT `the liability is only because of a new circumstance that has arisen since the prospectus or profile statement was lodged`)
        THEN NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "only because of a new circumstance that has arisen since the prospectus or the profile statement was lodged with the Authority"
        IF `the person proves that the person was not aware of the matter`
        THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "if the person proves that the person was not aware of the matter"

-- src:41371 | (7) For the purposes of this section, any reference to a statement
-- src:41372 | includes a reference to any information presented, regardless of
-- src:41373 | whether such information is in text or otherwise.
@ref s 255(7) (src:41371-41373)
GIVEN
    `the item is a statement` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the item a statement?
    `the item is information presented, whether in text or otherwise` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the item information presented, regardless of whether it is in text or otherwise?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 255(7) the item is a statement for the purposes of this section` MEANS
    IF `the item is a statement` OR `the item is information presented, whether in text or otherwise`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (includes): "any reference to a statement includes a reference to any information presented, regardless of whether such information is in text or otherwise"

-- the combiner: any defence proved is a defence; every paragraph answered JUST FALSE is "this section gives no defence on these facts" (never "no defence at all").
-- src:41295 | 255.—(1) A person referred to in section 253(4)(a), (b) or (c) is not
-- src:41296 | liable under section 253(1), and a person referred to in section 254(3)
-- src:41297 | is not liable under section 254(1), only because of a false or
-- src:41298 | misleading statement in a prospectus or a profile statement if the
-- src:41299 | person proves that the person —
@ref s 255 (the defences together) (src:41295-41299)
GIVEN
    `what section 255(1) answers` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN @desc What does the function `s 255(1) this section gives a defence for the false or misleading statement` answer for the person? (JUST TRUE, JUST FALSE, or NOTHING if you do not know.)
    `what section 255(2) answers` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN @desc What does the function `s 255(2) this section gives a defence for the omission` answer for the person? (JUST TRUE, JUST FALSE, or NOTHING if you do not know.)
    `what section 255(3) answers` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN @desc What does the function `s 255(3) this section gives a defence for reasonable reliance on information` answer for the person? (JUST TRUE, JUST FALSE, or NOTHING if you do not know.)
    `what section 255(5) answers` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN @desc What does the function `s 255(5) this section gives a defence for publicly withdrawing consent` answer for the person? (JUST TRUE, JUST FALSE, or NOTHING if you do not know.)
    `what section 255(6) answers` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN @desc What does the function `s 255(6) this section gives a defence for not being aware of a new circumstance` answer for the person? (JUST TRUE, JUST FALSE, or NOTHING if you do not know.)
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
-- FORK F53 (see NOTES.md, Fork register)
`s 255 the person has a defence` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF (`what section 255(1) answers` EQUALS JUST TRUE) OR (`what section 255(2) answers` EQUALS JUST TRUE) OR (`what section 255(3) answers` EQUALS JUST TRUE) OR (`what section 255(5) answers` EQUALS JUST TRUE) OR (`what section 255(6) answers` EQUALS JUST TRUE)
        THEN JUST TRUE
        IF (`what section 255(1) answers` EQUALS JUST FALSE) AND (`what section 255(2) answers` EQUALS JUST FALSE) AND (`what section 255(3) answers` EQUALS JUST FALSE) AND (`what section 255(5) answers` EQUALS JUST FALSE) AND (`what section 255(6) answers` EQUALS JUST FALSE)
        THEN JUST FALSE  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "if the person proves that the person"
        OTHERWISE NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (silent): one of the paragraphs was outside its scope or not worked out
